  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC Community Resilience in Masisi Territory and Lubero</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Build resilience through improved self -reliance and confidence of individuals and communities in their ability to prosper. This will be done by using their own influence on their local context, including protecting their rights, improving their income so that they can reinvest, establishing relationships between producers and traders, and increasing market access. Drawing on strategies combining protection and support for livelihoods, the project builds the foundations for transforming the context of chronic vulnerability and preventing adverse consequences of shocks linked to conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
